{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends","id":1271088,"title":"I'm 30+ yo roleplayer and have no friends","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-27T03:03:39-08:00","id":1271088,"title":"I'm 30+ yo roleplayer and have no friends","content":"Do you have the same? I just have gaming buddies that I called 'friends' few years before - but when in real life problems came to me it was only 'we can play', not real help or advise. Then I started to treasure world 'friend'. I now have few gaming buddies and two close female... Here I have problem of naming - they are not proper friends that may help you in every thing - but they can listen to you sometimes. And they can come to the party I make twice a year. Distant friends then?<br /> <br /> My partner is not my friend, in platonic way. Maybe I'm just lonely and why I'm oversharing on forum? Last 4 years I spent whole days alone - no real work colleages ( all in company are at least little conservative) , I see my partner only on weekends - and it's not even full weekends, as twice a month he has weekend studies whole days. Rest of time it's only me and my cats in home. From last year it's even harder - I moved outside of my home city and drive car 40 minutes one way, everyday. Now I live in small town, not even gaming club or rec center in it - so nothing to do after returning 'home'. I even like to wait and do over time in work to not be alone in empty home. \ud83d\ude14 When living in city I could at least go to fandom club and talk to other nerds. <br /> <br /> I try to run two chronicles on weekends ( the way they would not clash with free time with partner) - to fill loneliness. But I feel all my gaming buddies connections are fake, limited only to 'Karol, you are running the games for us - that's all'. \ud83d\ude1f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-27-2018, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:03:54-08:00","id":1271114,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry that you're feeling so lonely, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>. I can definitely relate to your situation (as can a few forumites I know). I'm one of those people that accidentally become the default ST/GM for their group of friends, most likely due to other people not wanting to do that level of work &quot;just&quot; to play a game. I'd show up to hang out, try to socialize (which I'm terrible at, but being lonely sucks), and eventually my social interactions would boil down to &quot;sooo, when can we play?&quot; It went on like that for years. In fact, that was my norm from age 13 until this past year (I'm 31 now).<br /> <br /> I have a group of people these days, though they're online (and some are here on the OPP forums hiding like ninjas.) I do my best to keep up with them, but I too find myself existentially lonely. It's hard to find a way to open up about my feeling when the people I want to share that with are primarily concerned with their own lives. I can understand that, though. Living, in and of itself, can be quite the journey. I only wish wish there were more companions to travel it with.<br /> <br /> I, personally, don't have any gaming outlets outside of running them myself, either. The last gaming store in my city was closed over a decade ago. I spent many an afternoon prowling that place and annoying the manager with requests for new d10s that I would pick out one-by-one as he watched with his beady eyes. Those were good years, but c'est la vie. Now, I'm mostly bored and probably boring. I run sporadic sessions of WoD games for my girlfriend, and occasionally get a word from my gaming group. It's a special kind of lonely. It reminds me of those moments where you're walking alone at night, and part of you wonders &quot;if I cried out for help, would anyone hear me?&quot; The scary part can be not knowing the true answer to that question. Do people think about me when I'm not doing something for them? Do they miss me when I'm not there? Do I really have friends at all?? Questions like that keep me up at night.<br /> <br /> I hope this comes off as me attempting to relate to your situation, and not some &quot;my problems are similar...BUT WORSE!&quot; rant. I know things are hard. Human beings are social animals, and to not have that socialization can be just as bad as an illness or injury. Loneliness hurts, in mind, body and spirit. It takes without giving back a thing, and I'm sorry that it's hurting you and taking from your happiness.<br /> <br /> If it's of any help, I'm online at least an hour a day, on one platform or another. I'm more than willing to make a new friend, and I like to listen. Feel free to DM me. I'll shower you with my contact information, so you can reach a friend any day you need one. *hugs the hamster*<br /> <br /> - Az","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:51:19-08:00","id":1271133,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I 'like' the post just because you offer companionship and I can totally relate. It says a lot. From age of circa 13 years old I was DM/ST/general GM of many groups. Did not have even stable 'friends' till get those with my then girlfriend, at age of 19-22 yo of my life. When we broke up, the group stayed mostly with her. I sustained my players, thinking about one of them as 'friend'. When having real life problems with my partner, he simply slide away and sustained our relationship only for me running games. Now I'm not fooling myself with people being real friend to me. MAYBE one old school distant friend can be related to this term - but I'm not sure. In RPG club, I'm just 'guy the runs games'. When I'm not seeing partner few days and not running any game - I wonder even if anyone really miss me. If I would not come to club, would they think about me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-27-2018, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T06:04:52-08:00","id":1273706,"title":"","content":"Hi Hamster, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This sad to read, but it\u00b4s not hopeless. Lonelyness is real for many people. The good thing is - you acknowledge it.<br /> <br /> Some modes you can try:<br /> <br /> Attend to something in your new homecity every 2nd weekend when your partner is not there.<br /> - Drive to you old city to meet up with people you like.<br /> - invite a or several gaming buddies to do something fun other than roleplay. are they really this closed off? Or is your lonelyness telling you that?<br /> - get to know some of your collegues better. Are they all this conservative? Or does their thing a t beeing a decent and fun human beeing trump their slightly conservative views. <br /> - Try to start a gaming group in your new home town but during the week, but don\u00b4t be the gm.<br /> - most importantly - talk to people: the weather, trains, nerdy things.<br /> - pe patient, do not judge yourself and please be nice to yourself!<br /> <br /> In the past I found a lot of help in these articles:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.succeedsocially.com/sociallife\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.succeedsocially.com/screenshot/succeedsociallyscreenimage.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.succeedsocially.com/sociallife\" target=\"_blank\"> How To Make Friends And Get A Social Life | www.succeedsocially.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.succeedsocially.com/sociallife\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.succeedsocially.com/sociallife </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A fairly common social issue people have is that they're not sure how to make friends and put together a social life for themselves. There are quite a few ways someone can find themselves in this situation... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T09:17:29-08:00","id":1273735,"title":"","content":"Hi, maekkel! Thanks for your voice. Only will answer on your points:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attend to something in your new homecity every 2nd weekend when your partner is not there.<br /> - Drive to you old city to meet up with people you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will run <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> game this weekend, when partner will be on studies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm very excited about it, almost purring with joy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- invite a or several gaming buddies to do something fun other than roleplay. are they really this closed off? Or is your lonelyness telling you that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to invite them to my last birthday party - come only one of them, and felt he do not come happy about party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- get to know some of your collegues better. Are they all this conservative? Or does their thing a t beeing a decent and fun human beeing trump their slightly conservative views.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like, about what can I talk with work collegues? They watch football ( I'm not interested ), they watch polish TV series ( that are awful in my POV ), the listen to our Disco Polo music genere ( after what I have literal headache and they use it sometimes as small 'torture' on me in work ). Lately I was small quarrel over my LGBT+ pins on my backpack. I have 'Marriage For All', my older colleague repeated all the time 'Marriage Not For All'. It was not some devastating attack on me - lived much worse things as local LGBT+ activist - but after 5 minutes of repeating like that I had a bad mood whole day and next one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try to start a gaming group in your new home town but during the week, but don\u00b4t be the gm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost impossible as I'm one of maybe 4-5 active GMs in city. ( Or in systems I'm interested to play. ) Probably could find Warhammer or Old World of Darkness games - but they are surely not something I will found fun, after all this years of playing them 'because I cannot play as player in other things'. My Mau player MAYBE run D&amp;D game - and then I may play with him. But it's very maybe...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- most importantly - talk to people: the weather, trains, nerdy things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk today with my work colleges about how my 'new' ( 10 year old ) car is always in repairs from buying of it. Been not very happier about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1273706#post1273706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- pe patient, do not judge yourself and please be nice to yourself!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, will be! Thanks for advice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-10-2018, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T00:43:08-08:00","id":1273849,"title":"","content":"Hi<br /> Your new games sounds fun. I hope it will be purrfect! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I\u00b4m sorry that your gaming buddies are so unresponsive. I still hope that with some time there can be some development. But I understand that in a small city this is tough.<br /> <br /> That your colleagues are this bad is stressful, i was hoping that at least some of them are decent people - even if they are conservative. but I did not know that they are reactionary Dupeks.<br /> <br /> The build up of a talking foundation can be tiresome, had similiar with my new colleagues, as the mood was quite sour and agressive. It took 6 months for them to soften up and constant friendly talk with continous openining up and finding common ground to have a relaxed atmosphere.<br /> <br /> I responded to your call, because it saddend me to see - that you as such a helpful and productive fellow forumite are feeling lonely.<br /> <br /> Best wishes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T21:39:37-08:00","id":1289413,"title":"","content":"Thanks for responses! <i>In a Nutshell</i>, great popular science series on YouTube, made video about Loneliness, how it's public heath problem - and that almost all people in age 18 till 50s are feeling it. Video shows some solution I advise you all to look for. Ironically, it points that RPG should help fight the Loneliness - how contrary is to the feelings of people in this topic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3Xv_g3g-mA\" data-code=\"n3Xv_g3g-mA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/n3Xv_g3g-mA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2019, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T21:48:32-08:00","id":1289418,"title":"","content":"If you feel sad and lonely, its ok. You ain't the only one that's feeling that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:29:55-08:00","id":1289759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1289418#post1289418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you feel sad and lonely, its ok. You ain't the only one that's feeling that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we should fight those feelings in the long way, yes? <i>In a Nutshell </i>video shows that long running Loneliness is <i>really</i> messing your life.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, I overcome it lately. I returned to my work, my LGBT+ activists actions ( like helping with 2nd Equality March in home city ) and running very positive game of <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> ( when still running Vikings <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> ). With coming Spring to our lands, I feel, finally, positive.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not 'I will go whole day to drink and talk with my buddies' - but it's get my batteries charged and I'm doing good things - i.e. helping in activists work and running good and possitive RPGs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:40:33-08:00","id":1289763,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, that maybe solution for some - In two last years I thrown myself into LGBT+ and prodemocratic activism. ( You may heard of problems in Poland with quasi-fasists government of PiS in late years. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> So joining my activism with RPG hobby, I started Facebook group called 'Rainbow RPGs' ( in Polish ) for people to talk about inclusiveness and their difficulties in hobby. We had slow start, but after almost a month of it's running, people are finally writing there with their problems and shareings, not only me and 2 other admins. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Building this community also lessen loneliness a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-03-2019, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:29:09-08:00","id":1289844,"title":"","content":"That is why I hated living in small towns, it can be so lonely. I\u2019m always happier in at least a moderately sized town, especially a college town because then I have people my age, though often younger, but friends five or eight years younger seem more likely to share my hobby then five or eight years older.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m happier if I game with people who I also like to hang out with, like cook dinner with and watch movies with. Before when I formed a group in college and even had weekly game nights were I would host and cook dinner, they essentially abandoned me when I burned my hand cooking them food... so I\u2019m more careful with friends...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T23:39:20-07:00","id":1328890,"title":"","content":"Development - In few days I have 32nd birthday. Tomorrow I'm doing a party for that. My partner that is all the time nagging I overthrow myself in LGBT+ activism, said to me to invite gaming buddies. Of course, they not coming. Any of four invited. \ud83d\ude1f Only my two female friends will be, I mentioned before, and my life partner. Maybe next year I invite LGBT+ activists - they seem at least honest people - not like RPG players...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2019, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T00:26:35-07:00","id":1328899,"title":"","content":"Well happy early birthday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T01:30:44-07:00","id":1333362,"title":"","content":"With your co-workers, I know you said that you're not interested in football - but there's a lot of basic connection that can occur at work just by simply asking someone what they thought of the past game - or if they're excited about the new season coming up. Where I'm at, I definitely feel on the outskirts of many of the social circles, but I push myself to make that small-talk about the local football/baseball teams even if I know nothing about them - and if a co-worker has a kid? Ask them how the kiddo is doing. Best way to make acquaintanceships with parents.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I would suggest investing in a hobby that isn't gaming. Something that takes you out of the house on a consistent basis to help combat the oppressive isolation that a lack of social connections can do. Hit up a local festival, or pick up a class being offered somewhere. You can meet people there who share some of your interests.<br /> <br /> Finding close friends as an adult is hard - and keeping them is even harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T22:49:04-07:00","id":1334300,"title":"","content":"Maybe my players are not so worst? Yesterday, one of player that was not on my birthdays give me this big teddy bear. It's almost twice funny, as in Polish, words for 'Master' and 'Bear' sounds somehow similar. So I got 'Game Bear', where I'm constant Game Master and also in Gay Bear minority in LGBT+ movement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's very fun and sweet from him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://scontent.frix7-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/69716618_10212633962318875_670035432414642176_n.jpg?_nc_cat=103&amp;_nc_oc=AQkH_67smkyrqXZbMedcuuakrg60pTtya2a-QAYLAS-Xdxa-qlOvVmBcLYLyxIa81M4&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.frix7-1.fna&amp;oh=8ee7f776b0468f5683152b9b85971828&amp;oe=5DF72BB5\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T22:11:03-07:00","id":1417599,"title":"","content":"Returning to the topic in times of COVID-19 pandemic - <b>How are you doing with long term Loneliness in hobby in times of pandemic? </b><br /> <br /> I try to organise things to have even buddies to play in multiplayer on computer and consoles - but it's not working. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I started private fan <a href=\"http://https//discord.gg/4fFqrwh\" target=\"_blank\">Discord server for Onyx Path fans in Europe</a> - but it's only mildly active. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I started private Discord for multiplayer gaming on PC and consoles with gaming buddies - but only 2 buddies joined it. As it seems, I'm just socially repulsive and alone outside my relationship. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I try to play on my Nintendo Switch, but I feel I need some REAL contact with people, outside of work - especially, with Lockdown over out near future in Poland.<br /> <br /> I try to play <i>Among Us</i> with Polish gay bear circle on PC - but I also feel as<i> outsider</i> there, as I REALLY do not know those people outside as avatars in <b>Bears of Poland</b> Facebook group... I REALLY need face to face RPG session - but even my planned Halloween special for <b>They Came From Beyond the Grave</b> will not come before the end of this month... And, of course, players are not readying and characters for it, so I'm not even can ease my mind, working over scenario...<br /> <br /> And now it rains outside... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T14:21:48-07:00","id":1419228,"title":"","content":"I just saw this cause I rarely post in the off-topic forum. I\u2019m an empath and I feel bad for you. You seem really nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T13:12:07-07:00","id":1420011,"title":"","content":"Thanks for kind words <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - two weeks later it seems to going in better direction. We paused our <b>Werewolf</b> game, as main plot is about magical sickness - nothing relly cool to run in global pandemic. However, I prepare <b>Scion</b> 2E game now, in vein of <i>Tomb Raider</i> series. starting in Ukraine. Our video game Discord server started to be semi-alive with Halloween events in games. And I pointed to mini-convention idea on the server in the times of proper spooky holiday. I also run <b>They Came From</b> one-shot on Halloween itself...<br /> <br /> So I got some hobby activities to plan and do - and as such, feel a bit less lonely. Yesterday 'session 0' for the <b>They Came From Beyond the Grave </b>was nice, and it recalled me my nerd buddies connections. Partner talked with our buddy over Discord for half an hour about Stephen King books - it was really cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even if slightly annoying, as we chat for the character creation for the game. But was cool, non the less.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2020, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T21:08:43-08:00","id":1428828,"title":"","content":"End is near! ( Of the year ) How are you nerds sticking in Xmas-New Years season? \ud83c\udf84<br /> <br /> I'm semi-hopeful. Got console games from my partner on early Xmas gift - <b>Immortals Fenyx Rising </b>and <b>Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity</b> - got holiday days from work from my boss (yupi!) - and preparing Xmas themes <b>Scion</b> one-shot on 26th of December to run. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( With <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/335850/Noel-Pantheon\" target=\"_blank\">Xmas Pantheon <b>Noel</b></a> by Oskar Eggertson! )<br /> <br /> I also <b>spinning Xmas and New Years related events</b> on our gaming Discord - but for now, have no ideas what to do... Any good ideas you have?<br /> <br /> Also, my new ongoing 'week-to-week' <b>Scion</b> chronicle, after 3 sessions, starts to get momentum. And nearing the rise of Atlantis! (spoilers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Overall, with games in slots and <b><i>some</i></b> reactions from my gamer buddies - world starts to look much more positive.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it seems as I mostly write on Discord and preparing games - rest of my group just hoops on when things are set by me. Well, at least we have fun, I see some new memes and hear new jokes when doing nerd things... It's at least <i>somewhat</i> hopefull, compared to 'sludging dread', only few weeks ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T22:05:43-08:00","id":1428832,"title":"","content":"I sent one of my friends a copy of Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity, and was looking to get Untitled Goose Game for my sister but couldn\u2019t find it. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T00:05:07-08:00","id":1428836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1428828#post1428828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">End is near! ( Of the year ) How are you nerds sticking in Xmas-New Years season? \ud83c\udf84<br /> <br /> I'm semi-hopeful. Got console games from my partner on early Xmas gift - <b>Immortals Fenyx Rising </b>and <b>Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity</b> - got holiday days from work from my boss (yupi!) - and preparing Xmas themes <b>Scion</b> one-shot on 26th of December to run. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( With <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/335850/Noel-Pantheon\" target=\"_blank\">Xmas Pantheon <b>Noel</b></a> by Oskar Eggertson! )<br /> <br /> I also <b>spinning Xmas and New Years related events</b> on our gaming Discord - but for now, have no ideas what to do... Any good ideas you have?<br /> <br /> Also, my new ongoing 'week-to-week' <b>Scion</b> chronicle, after 3 sessions, starts to get momentum. And nearing the rise of Atlantis! (spoilers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Overall, with games in slots and <b><i>some</i></b> reactions from my gamer buddies - world starts to look much more positive.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it seems as I mostly write on Discord and preparing games - rest of my group just hoops on when things are set by me. Well, at least we have fun, I see some new memes and hear new jokes when doing nerd things... It's at least <i>somewhat</i> hopefull, compared to 'sludging dread', only few weeks ago...</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is around Xmas and levity is needed, you could have Sanctacaris arrive from Canada. That's 'Santa Claws,' a fossil crab named by some scientists who were being silly. I have a crab necklace I got as a gift one Xmas and always remind everyone based on the famous Xmas letter, 'Yes, Virginia, There is a Santa Claus,' that there is a Santa Claws and that Santa Claws comes down from Canada (site of the North Pole). Maybe Santa Claws is there to help everyone open presents?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://burgess-shale.rom.on.ca/en/fossil-gallery/view-species.php?id=109&amp;m=1&amp;\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://burgess-shale.rom.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/ROM-Logo-white.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://burgess-shale.rom.on.ca/en/fossil-gallery/view-species.php?id=109&amp;m=1&amp;\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found - The Burgess Shale </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://burgess-shale.rom.on.ca/en/fossil-gallery/view-species.php?id=109&amp;m=1&amp;\" target=\"_blank\"> https://burgess-shale.rom.on.ca/en/fossil-gallery/view-species.php?id=109&amp;m=1&amp; </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While 2020 has had many horrible things happen, it's better as we get near the end than it was this spring and summer. We'll get through this with our gamer friends and other nice people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T08:36:30-07:00","id":1450958,"title":"","content":"<b>Returning half year later, I check with you, other lonely nerds there!</b><br /> <br /> In my life things are much better, even if got some a bit dread. I got semi-serious COVID infecion at start of April and even been in hospital for it for two weeks. Till this day I got some breathlessness, from time to time, but generally, healing helps and it's moving away. I also change departments in work for web development and become 'coordinator' of it ( junior manger ).<br /> <br /> As to topic semi topic - <b>Let's talk RPG online games. </b>I run constantly <b>Scion </b>2E and <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> alternating between them weekly for half a year now. They are both online only games now. ( Three players in two teams of 4 and 6 are from my local groups, but rest is online only meet people over internet. )<br /> <br /> But here is a thing - <b>What's with online game withdraw?</b><br /> <br /> <b>RoP </b>game is rather stable - only got one player to withdraw at early stage of character creation for campaign. But in <b>Scion</b>, i got a bit rotation. First local RPG club older buddy ( in age of my older brothers, after 40s ), second that was colleague of dedicated new player, now third player that joined to use 3 months ago, from United Kingdom. First because of larger work in life ( I understand ), second had apparently depression episodes ( or so she said ). Third left officially, because one of my constant, closes gamers buddies was late on three sessions - like 1-2 hours late. I can get he was irritated and on that game session went to party with his buddies in UK - I get that. I do not understand that after the late player apologized, UK player still suddenly left the team. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not with some drama, so my partner advised to just quietly let him, don't bother.<br /> <br /> So I made <b>second recruitment </b>for players in 3 months for <b>Scion</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It seems a bit strange. As it's my third in total in last half year, I see that from 4-6 people 'interested' in particular campaign, only 3 stays till proper game. <b>Doing character sheet for new game is a bit too much for most players?</b> It's my only requirement and test beside having the time for play. Or people that come forward to game are on 50:50 chances not thinking through their time commitment.<br /> <br /> <b>What do you think about players commitment to online game and leaving it just after few weeks?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-05-2021, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T20:05:34-07:00","id":1460170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1289413#post1289413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3Xv_g3g-mA\" data-code=\"n3Xv_g3g-mA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/n3Xv_g3g-mA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I love the videos of Kurzgesagt!<br /> <br /> And if you don't mind, I think your story shows a lot of how chronicle loneliness affects you in the way the video tells.<br /> <br /> You had a problem with the people you called &quot;friends&quot; in the past and then went into defensive mode. You built a strict definition of Friend as your armor, where you'll open up and be vulnerable only to someone that proves to be your Friend, but no one will approach you if you don't open up. You're an ST/GM. That means a group of people is whiling to reserve a chunk of their time regularly just to spend time with YOU and immerse themselves in YOUR ability to wove stories. This is a lot of social commitment right there, but your defensive state keep saying to you that this is not enough. Somehow they have to come to your birthday party. Why not just hang up a few hours after the game? Go watch a movie, or just go to a bar, even if you don't drink.<br /> <br /> That part in the video is true, when we feel lonely (been there for many years) you create defenses against social pain that only make you lonelier.<br /> <br /> On the question of player commitment online, this is always a hard bet, you're apparently doing fine. Seriously, it takes a lot of tries, it is what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:52:22-08:00","id":1467820,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I don't know if you still feel like this, but I hope things have improved. I'm in a similar situation, but I think I'm learning how to improve it bit by bit.<br /> <br /> My biggest problem was that when I was young, I went from having shitty friends or no friends at all to having a friend that I love more than a brother, someone who made me feel alive, fearless, and connected like no one else. Then years ago he had to leave to another country and since then I can't help but judge every new relationship based on what I had with him. Rationally, I know it's neither fair nor realistic to hold other people to such standards, but that lingering feeling of &quot;it's just not the same&quot; keeps following me. My solution was to understand that relationships are not a matter of all or nothing, there are different types with different intensities and each one brings something different that it's special in its own way. You have family, coworkers, gaming friends, classmates, and even the people you talk with in the forums. I still miss my best friend, and I don't think I will ever find a connection like the one I had with him, but that can't prevent me from enjoying other types of connections for what they are or even find one that is similar to what I had.<br /> <br /> I hope that my words help somehow, and I wish you a happy day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T02:50:21-08:00","id":1467863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1467820#post1467820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rationally, I know it's neither fair nor realistic to hold other people to such standards, but that lingering feeling of &quot;it's just not the same&quot; keeps following me. My solution was to understand that relationships are not a matter of all or nothing, there are different types with different intensities and each one brings something different that it's special in its own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that friendship is rare. But I still write I have problem with even more on casual 'good casual buddies that do not they ignore you, even on basic &lt;when we will have game night&gt;'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, my standards are even this low now... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Over past 2 years when I play online, I met some cool people - even when I did not seen them on my own eyes. I only know them on internet ( and voice chats of ours ) but they seem more like kindred spirits.<br /> <br /> On contrast, those that I meet from time to time IRL on our local gaming club - they failed me more than once. Right now I wonder if I should throw off from gaming group older gaming buddy, we played in RPG club for over 5 years now, with 2 of them on pandemic ( on online sessions, started from our gaming club ). He do not even answer on simple 'can you get on game session next week' massages on FB - 4th week in the row. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If he will not answer till tommorow, I will call him on his cellphone, to get the jist of what's happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2021, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T11:44:02-07:00","id":1478076,"title":"","content":"So the update on the subject... I'm started psychotherapy in mid of November of 2021 with depressing, overwhelming thoughts - 'autodestruktywne thoughts' we call them on therapy. Things like 'Maybe world will be better without me', you know. With coming Spring, I'm more and more optimistic - and this almost half year of therapy made me much more resistant to those negative feelings.<br /> <br /> With therapy, I try to reconcile I do not have friends. Maybe it was big depressing thoughts that made me seek 'true friends' - maybe I just get easier without them. I just run a lot of RPGs and try to change my work.<br /> <br /> Today got one big hope shot, in general - <b>There is Hope for Earth! </b>\ud83c\udf0f The world should not end as postapo wasteland because of Climate Change - it will be hard, but humanity should survive. Technology, trends and social changes from the last decade show that we CAN save our home - and remade the world! More information on <b>In a Nut Shell</b> channel<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As Climate Depression was one of fundamental sources of my thoughts - this science based essay is lifting my spirit, a lot! We CAN have future like in <b>TC </b><b>Aeon</b> or <b>Star Trek</b>! \ud83c\udf08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-05-2022, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T12:00:17-07:00","id":1478082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1478076#post1478076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today got one big hope shot, in general - <b>There is Hope for Earth! </b>\ud83c\udf0f The world should not end as postapo wasteland because of Climate Change - it will be hard, but humanity should survive. Technology, trends and social changes from the last decade show that we CAN save our home - and remade the world! More information on <b>In a Nut Shell</b> channel<br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/LxgMdjyw8uw</a></div> </div> </div> </div>As a nice coincidence I came here right after watching this new <b>Kurzgesagt</b> episode (they use the original name before the translation on other languages, so don't worry).<br /> <br /> I'm happy to know you're recovering. Things will get better. If you need medicine too, take it. But what's more important is that you're improving your mood and mental health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T16:00:07-07:00","id":1478097,"title":"","content":"At one time, I had to go through my phonebook and cross out all but about three names, because all everyone wanted to do was the same exact thing they had done the previous weekend, getting intoxicated. If you have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7SHwM1yeH0w\" target=\"_blank\">no friends</a>, any adventure that would normally involve a risk of losing friends can be undertaken without hesitation. There's a kind of courage that can come from solitude. I find that the best way to make new friends is to focus on what you bring to the exchange. What and how much are you willing to do for others, within reason? Being naturally curious about other people goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 04-05-2022, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T19:56:18-07:00","id":1478462,"title":"","content":"In my now 1,5 year Scion 2E game, I make 3rd recruitment phase for players. Like in clock, 9 months pass by - and even more stable players are going off the game. Why is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T00:33:23-07:00","id":1478474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1271088-i-m-30-yo-roleplayer-and-have-no-friends?p=1478462#post1478462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my now 1,5 year Scion 2E game, I make 3rd recruitment phase for players. Like in clock, 9 months pass by - and even more stable players are going off the game. Why is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably less about you or your game, and more about life moving on.<br /> <br /> There are many possible &quot;legitimate&quot; reasons for someone to have less time or focus on the game, and as time goes on the chance of one of those reasons coming to a particular player's life ceases being a statistical fluke to become a likelihood.<br /> <br /> In practice, keeping such regular groups for long is always hard because of the many factors that can interfere, and being a group activity means you multiply the likelihood of interference by the number of participants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T05:21:01-07:00","id":1478482,"title":"","content":"This happens to me a lot. Rn my rl D&amp;D group hasn\u2019t gotten together in several months cause we can\u2019t manage to get all of us together at once, so I play off and on when I can with my online group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}